From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:05:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5-ECAM's Switch side: its launch request in a file,
 etaHEN's jailbreak, the Lapy helper in eden/

PS5-ECAM 5.0.0's Switch games never started (its #67): it gave this program the game only as
LoadExec's arguments, which the console does not carry (MihawkOS saw argc 1 on every restart), and
under etaHEN this program had no /data.
- The arguments PS5-ECAM starts this program with are in /data/ps5cemu/eden/launch-request.txt too,
  one a line: taken once with filesystem access (forwarded_launch.h, TakeLaunchRequest), else the
  program's own arguments, as before. The boot trace says which.
- etaHEN's app jailbreak is asked first (/download0/etahen_jailbreak, the request PS5-ECAM makes for
  its own process, PPSA99360 being the title players list); when no HEN takes it within 2 s it is
  withdrawn and Lapy is asked as before (test_elevation.cpp).
- The Lapy helper is looked for in this program's folder, /app0/eden/lapy.elf, where PS5-ECAM
  packages it, then at /app0/lapy.elf.
